WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.890
In this demonstration I map an incident, event by event, to the seven phases of the Cyber Kill Chain,

2
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:11.966
and then find the earliest point where a Level 1 monitor could have stopped it.

3
00:00:11.966 --> 00:00:18.328
The case is a fictitious college, and it is different from the Payroll Email case in your activity.

4
00:00:19.427 --> 00:00:24.219
Here is the narrative: seven numbered events over four days at Sta.

5
00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:25.936
Elena Community College.

6
00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:30.083
I read it once from top to bottom before mapping anything.

7
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:34.969
Before mapping, I ask: which tool saw each event?

8
00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:40.841
grep dash N for the word log, colon, lists every event that came from a log,

9
00:00:40.841 --> 00:00:46.558
with its line number: the email gateway, the EDR twice, the proxy and DLP.

10
00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:49.185
Events 1 and 2 have no log at all.

11
00:00:49.185 --> 00:00:56.911
Reconnaissance and weaponization usually happen outside the victim's network, so we rarely see them.

12
00:00:58.011 --> 00:00:59.018
Now the map.

13
00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:06.066
Event 1, collecting staff emails from Facebook and the directory, is Reconnaissance.

14
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:11.183
Event 2, packing the JavaScript into a zip, is Weaponization.

15
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.868
Event 3, the email, is Delivery.

16
00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:20.580
Event 4, the user double-clicking and wscript running the file, is Exploitation.

17
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.453
Event 5, the scheduled task that runs at every logon, is Installation.

18
00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:31.822
Event 6, calling home every ten minutes, is Command and Control.

19
00:01:31.822 --> 00:01:37.443
And event 7, the student records leaving, is Actions on Objectives.

20
00:01:38.544 --> 00:01:43.412
Now the most important question: where could we have stopped it?

21
00:01:43.412 --> 00:01:49.726
At Delivery, the email gateway could have quarantined a zip that contains a script.

22
00:01:49.726 --> 00:01:56.725
And at Exploitation, at 08:26, the EDR saw wscript running a JavaScript file from Downloads.

23
00:01:56.725 --> 00:02:02.734
A Level 1 monitor who acts on that alert within minutes, and isolates REG-PC02,

24
00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:08.136
stops the attack more than a day before the data leaves on September 5.

25
00:02:09.736 --> 00:02:10.485
Your turn.

26
00:02:10.485 --> 00:02:14.533
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 3 and Activity 3.2.

27
00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:24.726
Read the Payroll Email narrative with cat tilde slash day3 slash Incident underscore Narrative underscore Kill underscore Chain dot txt.

28
00:02:24.726 --> 00:02:29.898
With your group, place every event in its phase, name the log source,

29
00:02:29.898 --> 00:02:34.696
and write the earliest point the attack could have been stopped.

